============================================================
32. IMPORTANT MISTAKES WE ENCOUNTERED
============================================================

MISTAKE 1:
----------

for i in salaries:
    print(salaries[i])


Why?

Because i contains the VALUE, not the index.

Correct:

for salary in salaries:
    print(salary)


MISTAKE 2:
----------

salary * 0.10

was initially treated as the new salary.

Actually:

salary * 0.10
    → bonus/raise amount

salary + salary * 0.10
    → new salary


MISTAKE 3:
----------

A function can be defined without executing.

Definition:

def calculate_bonus(...):
    ...


Execution:

calculate_bonus(75000, 0.10)


MISTAKE 4:
----------

Confusing set operations:

A & B
    → common

A - B
    → only A

A | B
    → everything


MISTAKE 5:
----------

Using dictionary variable name incorrectly.

If the variable is:

employee = {...}

Use:

employee["name"]

not:

employees["name"]


MISTAKE 6:
----------

Nested quotes inside an f-string.

Potentially problematic:

print(f"Department: {employee.get("department", "Unknown")}")


Safer:

print(f"Department: {employee.get('department', 'Unknown')}")


